Z||000000||JohnnyK||03-11-2001||09:29 PM||||I'm having this intermittent problem. 50% of the time, the temp guage will work, but the other times, it swings ALL the way to the right into the red. Now, I'm pretty sure it's electrical since it does that in the matter of 1 second.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The only problem is, I don't know where to look. Behind the instruments, it's just a circuit board with 2 or 3 plugs going into, so I assume there couldn't be a short there. Anyone else have ideas? Someone said the temp sending unit, but it seems to be up at the dash. Experiences?||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-12-2001||07:52 AM||||Well if you dont think that it is a short at the sensor, and you have found everything to be correct inside the dash, the possibly just your temp gauge is going bad.<P>I would doulbe check all the engine wiring though, it almost sounds like something is shorting to ground and your temp guage is set up so when there is 0 resistence, it reads hot.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||03-12-2001||12:47 PM||||And so the hunt begins. Wouldn't happen to know where the temp sensor is, would you?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||03-12-2001||03:33 PM||||The sending unit is on the engine.  On the V6's, it's on the LHS of aft corner of the aft head.  Has a 2-terminal connector (2 wires) on it - and often you'll find the connector shell is crumbled away from exhaust manifold heat.<P>...oops!  The above assumes we're talking about a <B>Fiero</B> van.  Hmmmm...  post some pictures of it, how about ?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 03-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||JBGehling||03-12-2001||07:27 PM||||Vans kick ass!||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||03-12-2001||10:31 PM||||LOL, I know i just bought an 96 Lumina loaded with 3800. just needed another vehicle to haul crap.<P>Temp sending unit is almost always on top of the intake manifold somewhere. Of course Fiero is not ! Some have 2 wires, some have 1 wire. Need to know what engine and vehicle is to tell ya for sure.||||reg||1
